 - **2026-10-10 (M5, shape fill colour, #686):** Rectangles, ovals, polygons and clouds can be filled. The comment quick bar has a Fill colour control for those tools ("No fill" or a swatch; it persists with the other per-tool styles), Comment Properties ▸ Appearance has a Fill colour row (one undo step with the other changes, carried over by Make Current Properties Default), and `comment_edit` takes `fill` (`"none"` removes it). `pdfcraft-annot::set_fill` writes or removes `/IC` and redraws the appearance; lines, ink and locked comments refuse it. Still missing: a custom colour picker (only the comment palette), and a separate fill for line endings.
 - **2026-10-10 (M10, #645):** Export all images and Save image as keep transparency. A JPEG with a soft mask (the usual cut-out photo) was written as the bare JPEG, and soft masks of another size than the image, JPEG-compressed soft masks, stencil `/Mask` images and colour-key `/Mask` arrays were dropped, so cut-outs came out on solid white or black. These images are now PNG with the mask as alpha (soft masks scaled to the image, `/Matte` un-blended); JPEGs without transparency are still written byte for byte. A negative image size no longer overflows in Save image as. JPX/JBIG2/CCITT masks are still left out. Overall estimate unchanged (about 30–35%).
 - **2026-10-10 (M12, XFA rows and areas):** Dynamic XFA forms lay out a repeating subform inside a top-to-bottom container in positioned content (a table in an area) with all its instances, drawn and measured, instead of one; and areas no longer appear in data paths (`pdfcraft_xfa::data_path`), since they are not data scopes. Before, a form whose fields sit in an area read none of the values Adobe's viewers saved, wrote what was filled here under a new element named after the area, which Adobe's viewers would most likely not read, and a FormCalc total looping over the table's rows failed on the rows that were missing. Layout, the script tree, reading and writing the data and the engine's value and row operations share the one path rule. Synthetic tests cover the layout, the path rule and the whole round trip (rows, Adobe-written values, a FormCalc total over all rows, the written data, reopening). Still open for such forms: XFA script objects (`<variables><script>`), which aren't supported. Overall estimate unchanged (about 30–35%).
